From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:42:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: Options held toggles the view, no default chords,
 and the history view off

No chord is on by default. The PSVR2 Sense pair has no Create
(visionOS gives the pair 32 elements and none is the one SDL maps to
Create), so Create plus L1 and Create plus Options never fired there,
and a held modifier delays the button it rides on. controls.txt can
still add a chord with chord.mod+btn=target, and recentre is head
look's, which is now off unless asked for.

The view toggle moves to a hold. A button can carry a hold target in
play: pressed, it waits; let go within half a second its own target
goes out as a tap, held past that the hold target goes out once as a
tap and the release sends nothing. Options holds togglecamera (z, the
game's own bind) by default, as one button on the right Sense half or
a DualSense, and a tap is still the game's menu, on the release.
controls.txt takes hold.btn=target for a key or a click, and =none
gives a button its press back. Each hold fired is logged with its
count.

The dialogue mark never showed after punching. The dialogue HUD's
Key_Event (sub_10555260) flips its history view on every mouse1 key
event (key 0xF1, through sub_10554B60), and the HUD hears every key, in
play as well as in a dialogue. With no dialogue active the pump now
turns that view off as the HUD's own setter does (the flag cleared, the
relayout flag at +0x190 raised), and in a dialogue a step closes it
before it marks. Single-line mode is the server's and is left alone. A
refused step logs why, once a dialogue.

Clicks stay plain presses and releases. Punches that seemed lost on the
headset were swings at nothing in reach, not dropped clicks.

The input self test covers five trigger pulls in play as plain clicks;
an Options tap as the menu on release and a hold as one z and no menu,
on the Sense pair and a DualSense, with hold.btn lines in controls.txt;
no chord by default, with the chord and recentre tests adding theirs as
controls.txt would; a history view left on outside a dialogue turned
off; and a step closing a dialogue's history and marking.
---
